so uh  i am raghavindran lakshmi narayan i'm a  research consultant and bioinformatics  mentor with bind biology uh it's very uh  it's wonderful to see you all and  welcome to this session  i'm trained in bioinformatics and i hold  a computational biology phd degree from  max prank institute germany so my  research interest and focus  is on the application of variety of data  science techniques such as machine  learning approaches deep learning  approaches towards the translational  studies of cancer biology towards  applying to plant genetics and  neurological disorder etc so my role in  this company includes mentoring a  variety of students like you students  who are from high school students who  are from bachelor's students were doing  masters and all the way up to students  who are pursuing phds  so  please let me introduce you about my  background and how we started in the  field of bioinformatics research  so the impact of human genome project in  a variety of biological research field  is very well known and documented so in  fact this very discussion that we are  having and the meeting is a result of  this extraordinary project  so this project affected my career as  well so when the findings of human  genome research project was announced  and its promise inspired me  to pursue a  career in biology  from  from jumping fields from being a  physicist  so i completed my master's in uh  biophysics and bioinformatics being  under graduation in uh being under  undergraduate in uh physics and followed  by which i joined max planck institute  in germany to  work on my phd thesis  so after that my two postdoctoral  research tenures from india from  institute of bioinformatics and applied  biotechnology bengaluru and jawaharlal  nehru university  this is where um it was instrumental in  helping me develop a deeper  understanding  in the  in the area of bioinformatics research  applications to variety of different  data sets so for the past eight months i  am part of this wonderful company which  gives me opportunity to share my  learning to inspiring students like you  so over the course of my career or over  the course of my tenure i have been  involved in projects from variety of  different backgrounds that includes  protein structural biology that includes  agriculture uh that includes multi-omics  data analysis like uh genomics  transcriptomics epigenomics data et  cetera and these are mixed data are  quite from a variety of different  sources like model systems  like from patient resources unlike from  agricultural sources and etc so this  variety of projects and this  wide spectrum has been immensely helpful  for me to tending to students with a  wide range of interest and in  in pursuing research training with  us so to give you an idea of uh  of my research uh interest and  background give let me share one of the  interesting projects that i was involved  in  during my career  so this is a project on precision  oncology and to introduce you to  precision oncology uh first let me tell  that  most of you would have already known  oncology is a study of cancer biology  and we know that cancer is a leading  cause of disease states worldwide for  such a dreadful disease and for disease  with such an impact um  systematic carrier treatments have  relied on drugs which are  chemotherapeutic drugs and these drugs  are marginally more toxic to the cancer  cells than normal studies i mean such an  approach is not very ideal and it gives  us our results in a huge problem  because on an average only 25 percentage  of the cancer patients respond  positively to these cancer products but  in comparison over 80 percentage of the  patients respond to popular painkillers  like  aspirin that you get over the count  so one of the prominent solution to this  problem is precision ontology so  precision ontological therapy is is a is  a strategy  where the treatment is actually designed  by targeting the molecular  characteristics of the patient's tumor  so hence the treatment that is given to  the patients are personalized to the  to those patients who are likely to  respond to specific therapies and  therapeutic approaches  so the way that we have approached or  the way that i have addressed this  precision oncological  problem issue  is to implement data-driven approaches  to include multi-omics data for  understanding and for predicting  patients response to a variety of cancer  treatments  so how do i do this  the tumor cells that that form cancer in  patients are  collected in during biopsy  and are then subjected to next  generation sequencing techniques and the  information about  gene expression the information about a  mutation and the information about  epigenetic variation that characterizes  the gene expression were extracted and  they were recorded  this data or these omics data  molecularly characterizes the tumor so  these are different from from  different types of tumor and different  subtypes of human and then these tumor  samples are then  grafted or then administered  several cancer drugs and their response  is studied by  measuring their bond  so this data records the tumors reaction  and response to different treatments  some for some treatments the tumor will  diminish in volume and for some of the  treatments it will not uh respond  positively so these responses and the  molecular  characterization data characterize data  were then integrated and various  machine learning algorithms and deep  learning algorithms were applied to  understand how they are related so from  this relationship we were able to  predict which patient or which cancer  from which patients  were able to positively or will be able  to respond positively to the treatment  that is that they are subjected to or  from the list of multiple treatments so  this is how we approach  understanding cancer biology from  multi-org data different approaches  so projects like these and various other  projects and  example projects methodologies and  resources are compiled and explained  expertly in the learn omix logic  platform so while you are enrolled in  specific programs that addresses your  interest you are also welcome to explore  various such resources under example  projects and expand your horizons in the  field of bioinformatics data analysis  so as i have already mentioned my main  involvement in this  is with the students  who are enrolled with research  fellowship program  this research fellowship program is  designed to address key challenges that  every student will face  while  subjecting or while opting for a  bioinformatic research so if you are  interested in extending your enrollment  for research fellowship program after  the completion of your specific program  then you would also  be able to leverage all the resources  that are developed to overcome these key  challenges like  time involved in learning and testing  out a lot of different strategies  and time and access to bioinformatics  expertise and access to  big data infrastructure  so  who will benefit from a research  fellowship program like this and who  what will the students like you take  away  from these research fellowship program  so for students who are new to  bioinformatics and who does not have an  early exposure to bioinformatics this  gives you an excellent opportunity to  develop an exposure to the methods to  the logic behind these methods and  analysis and to practice your knowledge  that we have gained  throughout this program  into a research project that interests  you or research project that will help  you in your care  and for students who have some exposure  to bioinformatics and who already know a  little bit of bioinformatics you will  gain expert feedback and project  evaluation  that will take your project from a  superficial investigation  to  superficial investigation  to a full-fledged research project that  fulfills many prominent criteria for  being a successful publication so you  will also be interacting with mentors  like me and dr mohit and elia and  understand where and how to find complex  data assets that is going to help you  design a very specific bioinformatics  project and this project as i have  already mentioned can be developed or  can be  designed with an aim to obtain a  research publication by the end of your  trend  so with that i will conclude my  presentation and i look forward to  interact with all of you during the  program and see most of you for the  research fellowship program  and what happened  yes so now i will pass the stage to dr  mohit mazundar to who will talk about  the highlights and curriculum of this  summer  [Music]

